-- The class itself. INSERT ... WHERE NOT EXISTS rather than INSERT OR IGNORE,
-- so re-running the script is a no-op instead of a silent partial write.
INSERT INTO imported_classes (class_id, name, system, markdown, status, created_by)
SELECT 'caf-scientist', 'CAF Scientist', 'rifts', '---
id: caf-scientist
name: CAF Scientist
system: rifts
category: occ
occ_group: optional
source_book: Rifts Dimension Book 2: Phase World p.60-61
attribute_requirements: { IQ: 12 }
starting_money: "2d6x100"
xp_table: [0, 2001, 4001, 8301, 16501, 25001, 35001, 50001, 70001, 95001, 130001, 180001, 230001, 280001, 330001]
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { name: "Computer Operation", bonus: 15, note: "+15% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Literacy: Native Language", bonus: 15, note: "Literacy, granted with the four languages below." }
    - { choose: 4, from: ["Language: Other"], bonus: 15, note: "Fluent in four languages of choice (+15%). The catalog''s repeatable Language: Other row is what an any-language pick resolves through - the whole Technical category is too wide, and Communications does not contain that row at all." }
    - { name: "Mathematics: Advanced", bonus: 20, note: "Printed as Advanced Math (+20%)." }
    - { name: "Radio: Basic", bonus: 10, note: "+10% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Basic Electronics", bonus: 10, note: "+10% bonus over base." }
    - { choose: 1, categories: ["Science"], bonus: 25, note: "One Science, the character''s specialty (+25%)." }
    - { name: "First Aid", bonus: 10, note: "+10% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "W.P. Energy Pistol", base: 0, per_level: 0 }
    - { name: "W.P. Energy Rifle", base: 0, per_level: 0 }
    - { name: "Hand to Hand: Basic", base: 0, per_level: 0, note: "May be changed to Expert at the cost of one O.C.C. Related skill, or to Martial Arts or Assassin at the cost of two." }
  occ_related_skills:
    count: 12
    categories:
      - { name: "Communications", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Domestic", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Electrical", bonus: 10 }
      - "Espionage"
      - { name: "Mechanical", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Medical", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Military", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Physical", except: ["Acrobatics"] }
      - { name: "Pilot", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Pilot Related", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Rogue", only: ["Computer Hacking"], bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Science", bonus: 20 }
      - { name: "Technical", bonus: 15 }
      - "Weapon Proficiencies"
      - "Wilderness"
    schedule: [{ level: 3, count: 2 }, { level: 6, count: 2 }, { level: 9, count: 2 }, { level: 12, count: 1 }]
    note: "Select 12 other skills, of which AT LEAST FOUR must be sciences, plus two more at levels three, six and nine and one at level twelve. All new skills start at level one proficiency. The four-science floor is a rule on the picks, which the app has no way to enforce; it is stated here and in extraction_notes."
  secondary_skills:
    count: 6
    schedule: [{ level: 4, count: 4 }]
    note: "Six secondary skills at level one and another four at level four, without the bonuses in parentheses, starting at the base skill level. The any/only/except limits above still apply."
equipment_starting:
  - { item_id: "hand-held-computer", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "portable-language-translator", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "toxic-analyzer", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "communicators-small", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "caf-battle-armor", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "hi-10-heavy-laser-pistol", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "portable-laboratory", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "first-aid-kit", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "dress-uniform", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "clothing", qty: 1 }
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan; the stat block runs from printed 60 onto
    printed 61 and both pages were read to the end. Everything from the
    Mechanical related-skill line to the Cybernetics line is on printed 61.
  - AT LEAST FOUR OF THE TWELVE RELATED SKILLS MUST BE SCIENCES. That is a
    constraint on the player''s picks, not on what the class offers, and nothing
    in the frontmatter can express it: `count` is a total and a category has no
    minimum. It is stated in the related-skills note so a player and a GM both
    see it, and enforcing it is a house rule until the app grows a per-category
    floor.
  - "CAF body armor" is read as the CAF Battle Armor of printed 120 rather than
    the CAF Jumpsuit of printed 119. The book distinguishes the two by name
    everywhere else it mentions them, and a Warrant Officer on a planetary survey
    is issued protection rather than a uniform; the jumpsuit is named as a
    uniform in its own entry. Flagged because it is a reading, not a quotation.
  - The book''s "analyzer" and "hand communicator" are generic. The catalog''s
    nearest rows are used - toxic-analyzer and communicators-small - rather than
    creating two more stubs for items the book gives no stats for.
  - occ_group is `optional`, matching the catalog''s rogue-scientist. The book
    calls these scientist soldiers and Warrant Officers with basic military
    training, but the trade is science: the class has no combat bonus block and
    its Military related skills carry the same +5% as its Medical ones.
  - Experience table transcribed from printed 183, this class''s own column.
---

## Lore

The CAF, and the Discovery Corps in particular, keeps a large number of
scientists aboard its ships. The Consortium deals constantly with unknown alien
species, unfamiliar weapon systems and threats nobody has classified yet, and
military specialists are often not enough - so a class of scientist soldiers was
folded into the military branch. They hold Warrant Officer rank: an officer''s
standing without command of a unit.

In the Discovery Corps they run planetary surveys, appraising worlds for
colonisation potential and examining local species to judge sentience, degree of
civilisation and likely pace of progress. They also study supernovas, black
holes and other astronomical phenomena.

They are trained across several scientific disciplines with one area of
specialisation, on top of basic military training.

## Friction with the line

CAF scientists routinely butt heads with conventional military officers, who
would rather destroy a potential danger than contain and study it. And many
scientists let curiosity get the better of them and undertake studies or
experiments that are outright dangerous. Most of the time the work is very
valuable to the Consortium anyway.

## GM Notes

Money is 2D6x100 credits and cybernetics are none. The class also carries
standing access to CAF military laboratories, computers, data files and other
research facilities, which is worth more than the equipment list and is not an
item.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'caf-scientist');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'caf-scientist';

